WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.520
Welcome to the Museum of Everyday Stories.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.797
I'm Clara, the curator.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:10.651
Our new exhibition opens soon, but its story cards have gone missing.

00:00:10.651 --> 00:00:16.941
Three objects are waiting on the table: a leather bag, a ceramic mug, and a wireless speaker.

00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:19.375
The bag belonged to a traveller.

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:22.752
Your job is to put the exhibition back together.

00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:27.608
The traveller was waiting at a station when she noticed something interesting.

00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:33.555
Some people were getting upset, but one calm, polite request changed the situation.

00:00:33.555 --> 00:00:38.608
She began collecting stories about ordinary objects and human behaviour.

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:43.196
She wanted to understand why small changes can make a big difference.

00:00:43.372 --> 00:00:48.415
Later, in a jungle, she watched a small lizard glide between trees.

00:00:48.365 --> 00:00:51.317
Another lizard stayed perfectly still.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.402
It made her think about our own reactions.

00:00:54.402 --> 00:00:57.607
Do we fight, run away, or freeze?

00:00:57.607 --> 00:01:03.325
Follow the clues, restore the missing words, and discover the message of her exhibition.

00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:04.734
Take your time.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.075
Every clue can be tried again.
